Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Configure all remote image hosts used by seeded data

Adds pollinations.ai (apex + subdomain wildcard, covering the
image.pollinations.ai generator) alongside the existing dicebear and
picsum hosts, and widens the Supabase Storage pattern from
/storage/v1/object/public/** to /storage/v1/** so image-transformation
(render) URLs are allowed too.

The Supabase host stays derived from NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL rather than
hardcoded, so each deployment allows its own project host.

Verified against the image optimizer: all configured hosts return
'url parameter is valid'; unconfigured hosts still return 400.

