From d9604dda0603c37b92951292e123bb0ce9feadf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Serve all demo imagery from local branded assets

The seed dataset pulled images from external providers (pollinations for
product/project/company imagery, dicebear for avatars) and legacy rows
still referenced picsum. That made demo content depend on third-party
uptime and leaked outbound requests on every page render.

Replace the whole pipeline with branded Medosha SVGs committed under
public/images (products, projects, companies, avatars, placeholders):

- scripts/lib/images.ts resolves each item to a local asset by category,
  keeping the existing keyword matching; unmatched items fall back to the
  branded placeholder for their kind.
- fictional.ts avatars now use the local avatar set instead of dicebear.
- next.config.ts drops every external host; Supabase Storage (derived from
  the environment) is the only permitted remote image source.
- Product/project/company cards render the branded placeholder when a
  record has no image, replacing the bare ImageOff icon.
- scripts/migrate-images.ts (npm run migrate:images) rewrites external
  URLs already stored in the database; dry run by default, --apply writes.

Verified: no external image URL remains in the repo, all mapped paths
resolve to files on disk, six pages load with zero requests to any
non-local host, and the production build passes.

